tion itself, so the version check and the\\\\n   227\\\\t// done/stale_discarded disposition stay in one place — the queue util.\\\\n   228\\\\texport interface HandlerDerivationWrite {\\\\n   229\\\\t  subjectKind: SubjectKind;\\\\n   230\\\\t  subjectId: string;\\\\n   231\\\\t  derivationType: DerivationType;\\\\n   232\\\\t  content: string;\\\\n   233\\\\t  metadata?: DerivationMetadata;\\\\n   234\\\\t  gaps?: DependencyGap[];\\\\n   235\\\\t}\\\\n   236\\\\t\\\\n   237\\\\t// The completion-transaction hook (Story 3): work that must land atomically\\\\n   238\\\\t// with the version-checked derivation writes — chunk placement and the\\\\n   239\\\\t// close→summary enqueues above all. The queue util invokes it inside the\\\\n   240\\\\t// completion's BEGIN IMMEDIATE, after the derivation writes and only when they hit\\\\n   241\\\\t// (a stale completion must not place a turn or enqueue summaries); onCommit\\\\n   242\\\\t// registrations flush after that COMMIT succeeds and drop on rollback, so a\\\\n   243\\\\t// crash leaves either a placed turn with its enqueues or nothing — never a\\\\n   244\\\\t// derived-but-unplaced turn.\\\\n   245\\\\texport interface CompletionTx {\\\\n   246\\\\t  db: DatabaseSync;\\\\n   247\\\\t  onCommit: (fn: () => void) => void;\\\\n   248\\\\t}\\\\n   249\\\\t\\\\n   250\\\\texport type HandlerOutcome =\\\\n   251\\\\t  | { ok: true; derivations?: HandlerDerivationWrite[]; onApplied?: (tx: CompletionTx) => void }\\\\n   252\\\\t  | { ok: false; retryable: boolean; reason: string }\\\\n   253\\\\t  | { ok: false; blocked: true; reason: string }; // source damage → derivation blocked, item terminal\\\\n   254\\\\t\\\\n   255\\\\t// item is the queue util's WorkItemRecord; typed structurally here so the\\\\n   256\\\\t// shared layer does not depend on the util's module (and vice versa stays\\\\n   257\\\\t// one-directional: tech-utils imports shared).\\\\n   258\\\\texport type WorkHandler = (\\\\n   259\\\\t  run: HandlerR