{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n \\\"Runtime|model_change|thinking_level|AC-6|runtime-change|runtime changes|constructed turns|typed blocks\\\" docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery -g '*.md'\"","aggregated_output":"docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:55:After this epic, every derivation has a deterministic floor and a uniform recovery cascade, so a not-ready or failed derivation degrades to an honest cruder rendering instead of blocking the operation or leaving a hole. Smart compact and turn construction always produce a usable result; only canonical source corruption stops them. Every fallback is recorded through a new logging surface so operators can see, query, and act on derivation health without runtime noise. Prompt smoothing gains a deterministic cleaning floor and a length gate; tool results split cleanly into deterministic full-band truncation and inference smooth-band summaries with per-tool guidance; the dead `tool_call_summary` type is removed; and runtime model/effort changes are recorded as typed blocks instead of opaque notes. The codebase is renamed from `form` to `derivation` throughout.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:66:- [Runtime-Change Typing](#6-runtime-change-typing) — typed model/effort change blocks. AC: 6.1–6.3\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:82:- Typed runtime-change blocks (`model_change`, `thinking_level_change`) replacing flattened `runtime_note` text for those events.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:266:A turn is constructed by composing its components into the turn renderings. Each derived component resolves through the recovery cascade: if its derivation is `ready`, use it; if not (`pending` or `failed`, handled the same), attempt recovery, fall to the deterministic floor, then to the original. The construction never blocks and never omits a span. Components that are not derived — assistant text, thinking, runtime-change blocks — are placed verbatim. Every fallback is logged (Flow 5). This is the contract from Onboarding Context, instantiated at the turn level.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:304:**AC-3.4:** Non-derived components (assistant text, assistant thinking, runtime-change blocks) are placed verbatim in the constructed turn.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:307:  - Given: a turn with assistant text, thinking, and a runtime-change block\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:483:### 6. Runtime-Change Typing\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:485:Runtime changes that occur mid-thread — model switches and thinking-level switches — are recorded as typed blocks (`model_change`, `thinking_level_change`) carrying structured fields, instead of being flattened into opaque `runtime_note` text. They are recorded at intake and projected as typed blocks; they are placed verbatim in constructed turns (Flow 3). Consumption of these blocks for host session restoration is out of scope (pi-lhc).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:489:**AC-6.1:** A model change is recorded and projected as a typed `model_change` block with structured fields (previous and new model).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:494:  - Then: a typed `model_change` block carries the previous and new model values\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:496:**AC-6.2:** A thinking-level change is recorded and projected as a typed `thinking_level_change` block with structured fields (previous and new level).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:501:  - Then: a typed `thinking_level_change` block carries the previous and new level values\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:503:**AC-6.3:** Typed runtime-change blocks are placed verbatim in constructed turns, in stream order, like other non-derived components.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:508:  - Then: both typed blocks appear unchanged and in order\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:556:### Typed Runtime-Change Blocks\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:560:| `model_change` | previousModel, newModel | Model switched mid-thread |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:561:| `thinking_level_change` | previousLevel, newLevel | Thinking level switched mid-thread |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:653:### Story 5: Runtime-change typing\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:655:**Delivers:** typed `model_change` / `thinking_level_change` blocks recorded at intake and placed verbatim in turns.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:656:**Governing idea:** preserve runtime-change structure instead of flattening to opaque text.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:660:- Flow 6: AC-6.1–6.3\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:675:- [x] Data contracts specified for states, tiers, logging surface, log entry, typed blocks\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/team-impl-log.md:24:6. 05-runtime-change-typing — Story 5: Runtime-Change Typing\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/team-impl-log.md:85:- Story 5: Runtime-change typed blocks (AC-6.1–6.3)\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/team-impl-log.md:89:- Test files: smoothing-recovery, tool-result-rendering, turn-cascade, chunk-compact-recovery, logging-surface, runtime-change-typing\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/team-impl-log.md:208:- Current Story: `05-runtime-change-typing`\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/team-impl-log.md:237:- Validation Artifact: `artifacts/05-runtime-change-typing/001-story-validate.json`\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/test-plan.md:73:| TC-3.4a | 3.4 | turn with assistant text, thinking