/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:266:A turn is constructed by composing its components into the turn renderings. Each derived component resolves through the recovery cascade: if its derivation is `ready`, use it; if not (`pending` or `failed`, handled the same), attempt recovery, fall to the deterministic floor, then to the original. The construction never blocks and never omits a span. Components that are not derived — assistant text, thinking, runtime-change blocks — are placed verbatim. Every fallback is logged (Flow 5). This is the contract from Onboarding Context, instantiated at the turn level.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:304:**AC-3.4:** Non-derived components (assistant text, assistant thinking, runtime-change blocks) are placed verbatim in the constructed turn.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:307:  - Given: a turn with assistant text, thinking, and a runtime-change block\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:483:### 6. Runtime-Change Typing\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:485:Runtime changes that occur mid-thread — model switches and thinking-level switches — are recorded as typed blocks (`model_change`, `thinking_level_change`) carrying structured fields, instead of being flattened into opaque `runtime_note` text. They are recorded at intake and projected as typed blocks; they are placed verbatim in constructed turns (Flow 3). Consumption of these blocks for host session restoration is out of scope (pi-lhc).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:489:**AC-6.1:** A model change is recorded and projected as a typed `model_change` block with structured fields (previous and new model).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:494:  - Then: a typed `model_change` block carries the previous and new model values\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:496:**AC-6.2:** A thinking-level change is recorded and projected as a typed `thinking_level_change` block with structured fields (previous and new level).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:501:  - Then: a typed `thinking_level_change` block carries the previous and new level values\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:503:**AC-6.3:** Typed runtime-change blocks are placed verbatim in constructed turns, in stream order, like other non-derived components.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:508:  - Then: both typed blocks appear unchanged and in order\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:556:### Typed Runtime-Change Blocks\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:560:| `model_change` | previousModel, newModel | Model switched mid-thread |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:561:| `thinking_level_change` | previousLevel, newLevel | Thinking level switched mid-thread |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:653:### Story 5: Runtime-change typing\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:655:**Delivers:** typed `model_change` / `thinking_level_change` blocks recorded at intake and placed verbatim in turns.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:656:**Governing idea:** preserve runtime-change structure instead of flattening to opaque text.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:660:- Flow 6: AC-6.1–6.3\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:675:- [x] Data contracts specified for states, tiers, logging surface, log entry, typed blocks\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/02-tool-result-rendering.md:123:- Runtime adapter: in-threshold summaries still use queued provider work, never hot path.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/01-prompt-smoothing.md:119:- Runtime adapter: under-cap inference still uses the existing provider path.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/coverage.md:43:| AC-6.1 | TC-6.1a | Story 5 |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/coverage.md:44:| AC-6.2 | TC-6.2a | Story 5 |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/coverage.md:45:| AC-6.3 | TC-6.3a | Story 5 |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/coverage.md:68:| Runtime model change | Model-change runtime event projects as typed `model_change` | Story 5 | TC-6.1a |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/coverage.md:69:| Runtime thinking change | Thinking-level runtime event projects as typed `thinking_level_change` | Story 5 | TC-6.2a |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/coverage.md:70:| Runtime turn placement | Typed runtime-change blocks place verbatim in constructed turns | Story 5 | TC-6.3a |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/coverage.md:81:| Story 5 | metadata / additive | Runtime-change events remain typed blocks through intake, projection, and turn construction. | None | intake/projection compatibility | Keep. |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/00-foundation.md:21:- Runtime surfacing mechanics in pi-lhc.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/05-runtime-change-typing.md:1:# Story 5: Runtime-Change Typing\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/05-runtime-change-typing.md:6:Record model and thinking-level changes as typed blocks and place them verbatim in constructed turns.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/05-runtime-change-typing.md:13:**Objective:** preserve runtime-change structure instead of flattening model and thinking-level changes into `runtime_note` text.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/05-runtime-change-typing.md:16:- `model_change` blocks with previous and new model.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/05-runtime-change-typing.md:17:- `thinking_level_change` blocks with previous and new level.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/05-runtime-change-typing.md:18:- Verbatim placement in cons